  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 240 AM MDT Sun Sep 27 2026\n\nWill see southwesterly flow aloft today and expect about 10\ndegrees of warming from yesterday ahead of an approaching\nPacific trof. Moisture will increase and expect isolated to\nscattered showers tonight and Monday with the most significant\nactivity in the eastern mountains. As the upper trof pushes east\nMonday will once again see cooling and about a 10 degree drop\nfrom today. Tuesday through next Sunday will be a dry period as\nwe enter an extended period of generally well above normal\ntemperatures as ridging will be the rule for quite some time.",
